Some people enjoy mostly "winning the game".  Good for them.  
Some people enjoy mostly "exploring the game".  Good for them.  
Some people enjoy mostly "finding abuses".  Good for them.  
Some people enjoy mostly "playing as it's intended".  Good for them.  
Some people enjoy mostly "playing in character".  Good for them.  

[Some people think their gaming preferences should be the 
default for the community, despising other opinions.  Not 
good for them ;-).]

The great thing about nethack ist that all of these 
kinds of players can enjoy playing nethack, playing 
completely differently.  To some, a character class 
is just defining some conditions, to some, it'll 
determine to some extent how they play.  Some try 
to find every loophole and exploit it, others try to 
avoid anything which could even look remotely like an 
abusive method.  All of them are welcome and valuable 
members of the nethack community and their comments, 
ideas and suggestion have added and will continue to 
add to the richness of nethack and rgrn.  

